Calc: retain manual row heights in point units

Only automatic heights keep the existing MSO 0.75pt quantization.
Rows and sheet defaults explicitly marked customHeight retain their
fractional point value. The old floor loses 23.2pt as 22.5pt and turns
0.5pt into zero, so a manual thin row becomes an automatic default row.

The existing point-to-twip conversion already bounds storage precision.
The synthetic MSO fixture and an otherwise identical non-MSO control
show that the truncation alone causes the geometry loss. The control
retains all seven manual heights, the custom default and nine formulas.
A rebuilt C++ engine still needs to run the new regression test.

diff --git a/sc/source/filter/oox/sheetdatacontext.cxx b/sc/source/filter/oox/sheetdatacontext.cxx
index 920f64d..00d05db 100644
--- a/sc/source/filter/oox/sheetdatacontext.cxx
+++ b/sc/source/filter/oox/sheetdatacontext.cxx
@@ -289,7 +289,7 @@ void SheetDataContext::importRow( const AttributeList& rAttribs )
     aModel.mbThickTop     = rAttribs.getBool( XML_thickTop, false );
     aModel.mbThickBottom  = rAttribs.getBool( XML_thickBot, false );
 
-    if (aModel.mfHeight > 0 && getFilter().isMSODocument())
+    if (aModel.mfHeight > 0 && !aModel.mbCustomHeight && getFilter().isMSODocument())
     {
         aModel.mfHeight -= fmod(aModel.mfHeight, 0.75);  //round down to 0.75pt
     }
diff --git a/sc/source/filter/oox/worksheetfragment.cxx b/sc/source/filter/oox/worksheetfragment.cxx
index 0b31247..55c9d7d 100644
--- a/sc/source/filter/oox/worksheetfragment.cxx
+++ b/sc/source/filter/oox/worksheetfragment.cxx
@@ -667,7 +667,7 @@ void WorksheetFragment::importSheetFormatPr( const AttributeList& rAttribs )
     // XML_outlineLevelCol
     // as it will be updated during export to OOXML
     double fDefaultRowHeight = rAttribs.getDouble(XML_defaultRowHeight, 0.0);
-    if (getFilter().isMSODocument())
+    if (!rAttribs.getBool(XML_customHeight, false) && getFilter().isMSODocument())
     {
         fDefaultRowHeight -= fmod(fDefaultRowHeight, 0.75);  //round down to 0.75pt
     }
